module nupp.system.spi

--[[Implementation interface for environment facts.

Importing this declaration loads no host implementation. Facts describe the executing Nupp ABI, including
emulated environments, and remain fixed for the loaded facade. Providers report
nonempty platform and architecture names, little or big endianness, and a 32- or
64-bit pointer width. They must agree with the target ABI used by generated code.

availableParallelism estimates the number of execution units usable by this
process, including host restrictions, and returns an integer of at least one.
It must not create a worker pool. The browser implementation may suspend while
requesting host facts. The facade chooses an external implementation by priority, then uses its native
or browser fallback when discovery is empty.
]]

--- Facts and a parallelism query for the executing ABI.
export interface Provider
    @readonly
    priority: integer?

    --- Platform name, such as macos, linux, windows, or browser.
    @readonly
    platform: string

    --- Architecture name, such as aarch64, x86_64, or wasm32.
    @readonly
    architecture: string

    --- Byte order: little or big.
    @readonly
    endianness: string

    --- Pointer width in bits: 32 or 64.
    @readonly
    pointerBits: integer

    --- Estimates usable execution units, always at least one.
    @readonly
    availableParallelism: function(): integer
end
